    'guard005-root-metadata-prep002/independent-fast-before-source-audit002/INDEPENDENT_FAST_BEFORE_SOURCE_DELTA_REVIEW_002.json',
    'guard005-root-metadata-prep002/independent-fast-before-source-audit002/INDEPENDENT_FAST_BEFORE_SOURCE_DELTA_REVIEW_002.md',
    'guard005-root-metadata-prep002/independent-fast-after-metadata-review-prep001/INDEPENDENT_AFTER_REVIEW_UTILITY_SOURCE_REVIEW_001.json',
    'guard005-root-metadata-prep002/independent-fast-after-metadata-review-prep001/INDEPENDENT_AFTER_REVIEW_UTILITY_SOURCE_REVIEW_002.json',
    'guard005-root-metadata-prep002/independent-fast-after-metadata-review-prep001/INDEPENDENT_AFTER_REVIEW_UTILITY_SOURCE_REVIEW_002.md',
    'ROOT_BOUNDED_PUBLISHER_NATIVE_SOURCE_CHOICE_008.json',
    'ROOT_SOURCE_CHOICE008_GUARD_SCOPE_PRECISION_009.json',
    'OWNER_WORK_WINDOW_30H_20261001_001.json',
]
for path in (before, copies, checkpoint, base / 'DOCS_REFRESH_AUDIT_026.json'):
    assert not path.exists(), str(path)
inputs = {name: (base / name).read_bytes() for name in names}
sha = lambda data: hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()
assert json.loads(inputs[names[2]])['verdict'] == 'PASS_DOCUMENTATION_FROZEN_CREATION_SCOPE_ONLY'
assert json.loads(inputs[names[5]])['verdict'] == 'PASS_STATIC_CONSUMER005_COMPLETE_SOURCE_AND_CAUSAL_TEST_PREPARATION_ONLY_WITH_PATH_AND_RUNTIME_LIMITS'
assert json.loads(inputs[names[17]])['verdict'] == 'PASS_STATIC_BEFORE006_EXPLICIT_TRANSITIVE_BINDING_EVIDENCE_DELTA_ONLY'
assert json.loads(inputs[names[20]])['verdict'] == 'PASS_STATIC_SOURCE_UTILITY_PREPARATION_ONLY'
now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)
assert now < datetime(2026, 10, 2, 22, 36, 15, tzinfo=timezone.utc)
stamp = now.isoformat(timespec='microseconds')
absent = [base / 'guard005-root-metadata-prep002/ROOT_METADATA_AUTHORIZATION_BEFORE_005.json',
          base / 'guard005-root-metadata-prep002/phase-before-005',
          base / 'consumer-guard-test-runtime005/ROOT_WHOLE_BEFORE_AUTHORIZATION_005.json',
          base / 'consumer-guard-test-runtime005/ROOT_EXECUTION_ACK_GUARD_UNIT005.json',
          base / 'consumer-guard-test-runtime005/ROOT_LAUNCH_START_005.json',
          root / '.tmp/cg14-005']
for path in absent:
    assert not path.exists(), str(path)

body = f'''# Major step026 - complete consumer source audit; isolated runtime preparations ready

Recorded {stamp}. The local/private owner window ends **2026-10-02T22:36:15Z**.

[Documentation025 peer](INDEPENDENT_DOCS_REFRESH_REVIEW_025.json) accepts its frozen
creation scope. Its primary history, selected copies and links remain preserved.
Later source reviews below do not retroactively change that earlier checkpoint.

[Complete Consumer005 source peer](consumer005-complete-static-audit001/INDEPENDENT_CONSUMER005_COMPLETE_SOURCE_REVIEW_001.json)
accepts source and causal test preparation only, with explicit Path and runtime
limits. It checked 1,737 unique finite inputs, all 884 declared payload files,
the manifest/post record, 847 preserved pairs and 14 selected active inputs.
All five consumers use explicit identity in the four type predicates; the
recursive bodies, imports, defaults, ordering, current Raw004 pins and other
guards remain unchanged. All 19 prior test method ASTs are exact. Five added
methods cover the M1-M4 causal routes and genuine controls. The two sibling
classes directly inherit unittest.TestCase: 19 + 5 prepared methods, without
inherited duplication. Actual collection and all 24 results remain unknown.
Existing Path isinstance semantics remain qualified. Finite declared closure
does not prove absence of unknown files. No reviewed target code ran.

[Consumer005 harness design](consumer005-isolated-unit-harness-design001/HARNESS_SOURCE_DESIGN_001.md)
is frozen, author-attributed DESIGN ONLY, awaiting a different peer and explicit
implementation choices. The old runner selects one class. Its source peer reader
expects 12 keys and at most 2 MiB; the new complete peer has 38 keys and 2,553,985
bytes. Three event families alone produce a hypothetical 780 passing events:
even an empty-namespace lower bound is 276,146 bytes, exceeding the unchanged
262,144-byte receipt cap by 14,002. This is source/data arithmetic, not a runtime
failure. Bounded complete event chunks are proposed; row grammar and source-peer
reader choices remain pending. No cap increase, harness implementation, binding
or execution is approved by this design.

[BEFORE006 delta peer](guard005-root-metadata-prep002/independent-fast-before-source-audit002/INDEPENDENT_FAST_BEFORE_SOURCE_DELTA_REVIEW_002.json)
accepts only the explicit transitive binding-evidence delta over the preserved
full BEFORE005 review. [AFTER002 source peer](guard005-root-metadata-prep002/independent-fast-after-metadata-review-prep001/INDEPENDENT_AFTER_REVIEW_UTILITY_SOURCE_REVIEW_002.json)
accepts source utility preparation only. AFTER001's wrong-class/namespace,
ordered ACK source and missing transitive evidence refusals are preserved.
The corrected utilities carry source binding d8f77 and phase binding 11384 with
the independently reviewed four PowerShell sources. They return data; genuine
actual producer attribution, nominal closed approval cores, physical tool trace,
freshness and Root execution decisions remain separate. Their mains are UNRUN.

The next permitted concrete runtime workflow is the already prepared GG5
**14-method copied baseline**, using old Consumer003 and its exact source peer.
It will not validate current Raw004, Consumer005, publication or native readiness.
Fresh Metadata002 authorization, capture, whole inventories, ACK, bound/late
reviews and unit receipts remain ABSENT. Readiness callbacks and commands must
be complete before starting the original 600-second context timer. Bound/late
context age must be at most 90 seconds; Root reserves 450 seconds for the unit
and 60 seconds for after checks. Resources must be at most 60 seconds old through
spawn. No retimestamp, lifetime extension or replay is allowed. Fix all primary
docs during the before/unit/after proof interval, then publish the actual result.

The workflow distinguishes metadata authorization17/capture14/parent20, whole
authorization15/result19/parent30, driver finished20 and physical Root terminal18.
Whole after checks keep the original before runtime/context hashes and the
byte-identical finished receipt bridge. Metadata after has its own fresh context
and links the original capture and physical unit terminal. GG5 emits collection,
result and transcript/events/subtests; it emits no JUnit/XML. Current Raw00458,
Consumer00524, metadata24 plus two probes, and Native111 tests remain UNRUN.
Old Metadata001 remains spent/expired and immutable.

[Gate009 finite observation](gate009-finite-readonly-observation002/FINITE_GATE009_OBSERVATION_002.md)
at 11:55:18.314283 UTC found unchanged selected source/test/release bytes, one
accepted 13-node governance partition and the two terminal heavy failures.
44 partitions/5,562 planned nodes remain unaccepted. The known folder had six
unchanged names; fixed continuation002/new acceptance/finish paths were absent.
This is finite timed evidence, not a global process, full742/263 or failure-cause
proof. No sole-executor ACK, delivered transfer, lease or native quiet is established.
Canonical live apply/full QA/new gate/commit/release/native and Pro3 holds persist.

Bootstrap is still authoring the distinct bounded publication/native package
under [Root008](ROOT_BOUNDED_PUBLISHER_NATIVE_SOURCE_CHOICE_008.json) and
[scope precision009](ROOT_SOURCE_CHOICE008_GUARD_SCOPE_PRECISION_009.json).
Its latest author report describes the complete 31-fact typed witness as 32,489
bytes/578 nodes, superseding the earlier eleven-fact advisory size for current
design work. Its current common draft is 178,891 bytes and is not frozen or
accepted. Two ordered schema3 acquisitions, bounded acquisition derivation,
entry ordering, current causal fixtures and a complete different source audit
remain ahead. Hard limits stay common184317/growth5731/frame262142, binding16384
encoded/12288 decoded, 44 fields/35 hashes/17 path roles, API12/seven raw roles,
global395799/private361287. Actual path/OS command/runtime slots remain None.
Source improvements authorize no operational binding, live apply or native run.

Preserve frozen science, incident/terminal twins, the existing recovery epoch,
attempt012 and every consumed helper, reserves, original piped GO/noNonInteractive,
83/84 history, no public action/push/replay/extra epoch or guard reduction.
Recovery111 fits require accepted proofs; seal precedes downstream fits. No
unrelated process was stopped. Keeper launch remains consumed and monitor
